# Copy this file to .env for local dev, then fill in your real keys.
# NEVER commit your real .env file — it's already in .gitignore.
#
# WARNING: These are VITE_-prefixed on purpose: Vite exposes any VITE_
# variable directly to the browser bundle. That's required for the current
# DIRECT client-side integration (see README.md "Direct vs Hidden
# Integration"). It also means these keys are visible to anyone who
# inspects your deployed site's network requests or JS bundle — restrict
# them (see below) before publishing publicly.

# Google AI Studio API key — powers Kanuu, the chat assistant.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys
# Recommended: restrict it to "Generative Language API" only, and add an
# HTTP referrer restriction for your deployed domain once you have one.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# OpenWeatherMap API key — lets Kanuu answer weather questions.
# Get one at https://openweathermap.org/api
VITE_OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=your_openweather_api_key_here
